  "reference": "Ecclesiastes 3",
  "verseCount": 15,
  "content": [
    {
      "name": "chapter",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "number": "3",
        "style": "c",
        "sid": "ECC 3"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "3",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "1",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:1"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "1",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For everything there is a season, and a time for every matter under heaven:",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.1",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.1"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "9",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:9"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "9",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.9",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.9"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "10",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:10"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "10",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I have seen the business that God has given to the sons of men to be busy with. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.10",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.10"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "11",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:11"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "11",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "He has made everything beautiful in its time; also he has put eternity into man's mind, yet so that he cannot find out what God has done from the beginning to the end. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.11",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.11"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "12",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:12"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "12",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I know that there is nothing better for them than to be happy and enjoy themselves as long as they live; ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.12",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.12"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "13",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:13"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "13",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "also that it is God's gift to man that every one should eat and drink and take pleasure in all his toil. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.13",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.13"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I know that whatever God does endures for ever; nothing can be added to it, nor anything taken from it; God has made it so, in order that men should fear before him. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "That which is, already has been; that which is to be, already has been; and God seeks what has been driven away.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.15"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Moreover I saw under the sun that in the place of justice, even there was wickedness, and in the place of righteousness, even there was wickedness. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I said in my heart, God will judge the righteous and the wicked, for he has appointed a time for every matter, and for every work. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "I said in my heart with regard to the sons of men that God is testing them to show them that they are but beasts. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For the fate of the sons of men and the fate of beasts is the same; as one dies, so dies the other. They all have the same breath, and man has no advantage over the beasts; for all is vanity. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "All go to one place; all are from the dust, and all turn to dust again. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Who knows whether the spirit of man goes upward and the spirit of the beast goes down to the earth? ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "ECC 3:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "So I saw that there is nothing better than that a man should enjoy his work, for that is his lot; who can bring him to see what will be after him?",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "ECC.3.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "ECC.3.22"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "next": {
    "id": "ECC.4",
    "number": "4",
    "bookId": "ECC"
  },
  "previous": {
    "id": "ECC.2",
